loom_public_page('Privacy','A default privacy overview for LOOM installations. Deployment owners should customize this notice for their own organization, jurisdiction, integrations, and data practices.',
'<section class="card"><h2>What LOOM can store</h2><p>Depending on enabled modules and installation settings, LOOM can persist guest identities, permanent account details, project identities, project state, activity/audit records, referral attribution, uploaded assets, administrative configuration, and continuity metadata used to recognize a likely returning anonymous guest across browser contexts.</p></section><section class="card"><h2>Anonymous continuity</h2><p>LOOM can compare coarse browser/device traits together with already-recorded network metadata to decide whether a fresh browser is very likely to continue one recent, unclaimed Guest Identity. LOOM stores normalized hashes rather than a raw permanent hardware identifier, refuses automatic recovery when a device appears shared or the current network differs, and never treats continuity as authentication. Permanent-account, Admin, purchase, private-message, and other authenticated authority still require durable verification.</p></section><section class="card"><h2>Sharing and referrals</h2><p>Attributed share links contain an opaque referral code. A link is reusable and may be opened by many people. Opening your own share link is recorded as a self-visit but does not consume or disable the link and never earns referral credit. When a recipient follows one, LOOM can record the referring identity, destination, link-open counts, and a durable referral relationship after the recipient selects or creates a LOOM identity. Referral codes do not contain the referrer’s email or password.</p></section><section class="card"><h2>Deployment owner responsibility</h2><p>LOOM is deployable software. The operator of a particular LOOM installation controls its hosting, connected services, retention policies, user access, and legal notices. This packaged notice is a technical baseline, not a substitute for deployment-specific legal review.</p></section>','privacy');
